---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";

/** noindex for the same reason as /privacy/: it has to exist and be linked,
    not rank. */

const updated = "22 September 2026";
---

<Base
  title={`Terms & Conditions — ${SITE.name}`}
  description="The terms you accept by using this site, and how they relate to paid work, bootcamps and the newsletter."
  noindex
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <span class="kicker">Legal</span>
      <h1 class="page-head__title">Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
      <p class="page-head__lede">
        The terms you accept by using this site, and where a separate agreement takes over
        instead.
      </p>
      <p class="post__date">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose--narrow">
      <h2>Who these terms are with</h2>
      <p>
        This site is operated by {SITE.name}, {SITE.jobTitle}, based in {SITE.locality},
        {SITE.countryName} — "I" and "me" throughout. Using the site means accepting these terms.
        If you do not accept them, please stop using it.
      </p>
      <p>
        <mark
          >REVIEW: if you trade under a registered business name, name it and its registered
          address here so the contracting party is unambiguous.</mark
        >
      </p>

      <h2>The site is information, not an offer</h2>
      <p>
        The services, packages, prices and results described here are for information. Nothing on
        this site is a binding offer, and publishing a price does not oblige me to accept a
        project at it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Paid work begins only when we have both agreed a scope in writing — a proposal, statement
        of work or contract. <strong>Where that agreement and these terms disagree, that
        agreement wins.</strong>
      </p>

      <h2>Case studies and results</h2>
      <p>
        The outcomes shown in case studies and use cases happened for those clients, in their
        markets, with their budgets and constraints. They are evidence of what I have done, not a
        forecast of what your project will do. Search and advertising results depend on factors
        outside my control, and I do not guarantee rankings, traffic or revenue.
      </p>

      <h2>Using the site</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>submit false information or somebody else's personal details through the forms;</li>
        <li>attempt to break, overload or gain unauthorised access to the site or its server;</li>
        <li>scrape it in a way that degrades it for other people;</li>
        <li>use the contact form or newsletter to send unsolicited commercial messages.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Forms are rate-limited and protected against automated abuse. I may block access that
        breaches these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The text, design, code, images and video on this site are mine, or used with permission,
        and are protected by copyright. Client names and logos belong to their owners and appear
        with their agreement.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may read, link to and quote short extracts with attribution. You may not republish
        substantial parts, or pass the work off as your own, without written permission. Rights in
        work produced under a client engagement are governed by that engagement, not by this page.
      </p>

      <h2>The newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        Subscribing is free and confirmed by email before anything is sent. Every issue carries an
        unsubscribe link that works immediately. I may change how often it goes out, or stop
        sending it.
      </p>

      <h2>Bootcamps and the community</h2>
      <p>
        Bootcamps and the community are described here ahead of opening, and those descriptions may
        change before they launch. Joining either is subject to its own terms and pricing at the
        time you enrol, together with the terms of any third-party platform it runs on — the
        community is planned for Skool, which has its own terms and privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        Links to other sites are there because they were useful. I do not control them and am not
        responsible for their content, their terms or how they handle your data.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability and liability</h2>
      <p>
        I keep the site up and accurate, but I do not promise it will be uninterrupted, error-free,
        or right at every moment. It is provided as it is.
      </p>
      <p>
        To the extent the law allows, I am not liable for indirect or consequential loss, lost
        profit, lost revenue or lost data arising from your use of this site.
        <strong
          >Nothing here limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for
          fraud, or for anything else that cannot lawfully be limited.</strong
        > Liability for paid work is governed by our written agreement.
        <mark
          >REVIEW: have a lawyer confirm this clause is enforceable in your jurisdiction and
          against the consumers you sell to — liability caps are the part most often struck
          out.</mark
        >
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        How this site handles personal data is set out in the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>,
        which forms part of these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        I may update these terms. The date at the top shows when they last changed, and the version
        published here is the one that applies to your visit.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        <mark
          >REVIEW: name the governing law and the courts that have jurisdiction. Selling to EU
          consumers limits how far you can override the protections of their home country, so
          this is worth getting right rather than guessing.</mark
        >
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms:
        <a href="mailto:kastriot@kastriottanaj.com">kastriot@kastriottanaj.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
